{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 22, :comments ["<b>And when you reap the harvest, etc.</b> What does this matter have to do here? Perhaps it comes to obligate even the field from which the omer was brought — that it is obligated in gleanings (leket) and the corner (pe'ah), for one might reason: since its beginning was reaped for an offering, it should be exempt from pe'ah, and so forth — therefore Scripture states it. And accordingly you will find that He mentioned only leket and pe'ah, which are obligations of the field without any intermediary circumstance, whereas forgotten sheaves (shikh'ḥah), which comes from the side of the owner of the field, was not mentioned. And in Torat Kohanim they said that HaShem hinted through this that whoever gives leket, shikh'ḥah, and pe'ah, it is accounted to him as though the Temple were standing and he were bringing his offerings into it, and so forth — end quote. That which they said shikh'ḥah even though it was not mentioned in the verse is because it is a commandment one is obligated in just like leket and pe'ah, so it is included. And the verse did not write it in order to alert you that the intent is also toward the approach I have written."], :book :leviticus, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 23, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T20:00:28.829816221Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}